#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/rust.md:6
msgid "Unsafe Rust Functions"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/rust.md:8
msgid ""
"You can mark your own functions as `unsafe` if they require particular "
"preconditions to avoid undefined behaviour."
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/rust.md:12
msgid "// Copyright 2025 Google LLC\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/rust.md:13
msgid "// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/rust.md:14
msgid ""
"/// Swaps the values pointed to by the given pointers.\n"
"///\n"
"/// # Safety\n"
"///\n"
"/// The pointers must be valid, properly aligned, and not otherwise accessed "
"for\n"
"/// the duration of the function call.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/rust.md:22
msgid ""
"// SAFETY: Our caller promised that the pointers are valid, properly "
"aligned\n"
"    // and have no other access.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/rust.md:35
msgid ""
"// SAFETY: The pointers must be valid, aligned and unique because they came\n"
"    // from references.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/rust.md:41
msgid "\"a = {}, b = {}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/rust.md:47
msgid ""
"We wouldn't actually use pointers for a `swap` function --- it can be done "
"safely with references."
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/unsafe-functions/rust.md:50
msgid ""
"Note that Rust 2021 and earlier allow unsafe code within an unsafe function "
"without an `unsafe` block. This changed in the 2024 edition. We can prohibit "
"it in older editions with `#[deny(unsafe_op_in_unsafe_fn)]`. Try adding it "
"and see what happens."
msgstr ""
